  "query_preview": "..(This Evening Through Tuesday)\nIssued at 249 PM MST Tue Nov 24 2026\n\nCurrent water vapor and upper air analysis depicts ridge over the\nwestern US with troughing over the central US. A moisture starved\nshortwave/developing upper low sits over SK/ND border. Our corner\nof the Northern Plains sits under partly cloudy skies with \ntemperatures in the mid 30s to mid 40s. The developing upper low \nwill slide southeast overnight with minimal weather impacts felt \nat the surface. CAMs and forecast soundings show low level \nmoisture and some light upslope flow which will support the \ndevelopment of fog over much of the western SD plains. The fog \nshould have the greatest coverage towards central SD with patchy \nfog further west.\n\nRidging builds over the region tomorrow in the wake of the \ndeparting upper low with southerly return flow supporting WAA and \na gradual warming trend through Friday. The weather on \nThanksgiving Day will be pleasant with highs in the upper 40s to \nlow 50s, light winds, and partly cloudy skies.\n\nOur next system moves through the area during the day Friday. An \nupper low will pass to the north of the CWA with an attendant cold\nfront pushing through the area Friday morning. This front will \nbring breezy west to northwest winds (max gusts of 40-50 mph) to \nnorthwestern SD for Friday afternoon. Light rain/snow may move \nthrough northeastern WY into the Black Hills and southwestern SD \nlate Friday night/Saturday morning though QPF amounts are looking \npretty light at this point in time.",
